  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Livelihood Support to the most vulnerable populations affected by the floods in Lakes, Northern Bahr el Ghazal, Upper Nile, Central Equatoria and Eastern Equatoria States in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the most vulnerable to maintain or resume food production by providing lifesaving support to flood affected
vulnerable populations. Activities will revolve around the timely provision of inputs necessary to engage in crop, vegetable and fisheries
production and protect livestock assets. FAO?s livelihood kits are designed to be easily portable, provide maximum nutritional value and
minimize time to harvest</narrative>
  </description>
